{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ea24d1cd-aff9-477a-8f33-d734d9e988e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c46e9e8af2d08e7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-un3gt0h0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E001.md","content":"# Run comparison view in the Dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nDeliver a run comparison surface in the Dashboard: users can select two or\nmore training and pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics side by\nside, and, for two selected runs, switch to a diff presentation that highlights\nwhich parameters and metrics changed. This replaces the current workflow of\nexporting run data to spreadsheets for comparison.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Run selection from the runs list: a user can select two or more runs and\n  open the comparison.\n- Side-by-side presentation of each selected run's parameters and metrics in a\n  single comparison view.\n- Diff presentation for two selected runs: values that differ between the two\n  runs are highlighted so changed parameters and metrics are immediately\n  visible; unchanged values remain distinguishable.\n- The comparison reads run parameters and metrics through the Dashboard's\n  existing run data sources (including the KFP v2 interface for pipeline\n  runs); no changes to the run-producing backends are in scope.\n- The comparison works for both training runs and pipeline runs within a\n  project. Comparison across clusters or across projects is out of scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a list of runs, when a user selects two or more runs and opens the\n  comparison, then the parameters and metrics of every selected run are\n  displayed side by side in a single view.\n- Given two runs displayed in the comparison, when the user switches to the\n  diff presentation, then the parameters and metrics that differ between the\n  two runs are highlighted and unchanged values are distinguishable.\n- Given pipeline runs and training runs in the same project, when either kind\n  is included in a selection, then their parameters and metrics are retrieved\n  through the existing run data interfaces and rendered in the comparison.\n- Given a selection that includes a run with missing parameters or metrics,\n  then the comparison renders the available values without failing the whole\n  view.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: select two or more runs and view their parameters and\n  metrics side by side in the Dashboard — fully covered by this epic.\n- **HLR-3 (P1, bundled)**: the run \"diff\" view highlighting which parameters\n  and metrics changed between two selected runs is a presentation mode of the\n  same comparison surface over the same run data, in the same component and\n  team — bundled into this epic at the higher priority (P0) rather than split\n  into a separate epic, because splitting would build the same surface twice\n  and add an artificial serialization boundary.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41040,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8421bd3d5321a850","agent_id":"aebebc7cfbe226f9e","session_id":"56ee33b5-80f9-4b38-b563-1eee8ceebc36","uuid":"3cccee3a-0f8e-4274-82f0-60595df06d4a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:14:38.603Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
