{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cac1ee17-0e52-4100-b7a9-a93a88675b50","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-84da6fb3ac8542a4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-un3gt0h0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E003.md","content":"# Run lineage on registered model versions\n\n## Description\n\nRegistered model versions record the run that produced them, and that linkage\nis exposed through the Model Registry so clients can resolve the producing run\nfor a given model version. This is the data foundation that lets a comparison\nbe opened starting from the Model Registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Capture the producing-run reference on a registered model version at\n  registration time, when the producing run is known.\n- Expose the producing-run linkage as model version metadata through the Model\n  Registry's existing metadata extension point (custom properties on model\n  versions, per the architecture context), so clients can retrieve it for a\n  given model version.\n- Keep registration backward compatible: model versions registered without run\n  information remain valid and fully functional.\n- Out of scope: automatic best-run selection or promotion, and any comparison\n  logic (the comparison surface itself lives in the Dashboard).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered from a known run, then the producing run's\n  reference is recorded on the model version and retrievable through the Model\n  Registry interface by a client that knows only the model version.\n- Given a model version registered without run information, then registration\n  succeeds and the model version remains valid and queryable.\n- Given an existing model version registered before this change, then it\n  remains valid and readable with no migration required.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1, data half)**: \"registered model versions link back to the run\n  that produced them\" — the linkage data and its exposure are delivered by\n  this epic. The registry-side entry point that opens a comparison from this\n  linkage is the Dashboard's registry integration and is covered separately.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42571,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8421bd3d5321a850","agent_id":"aebebc7cfbe226f9e","session_id":"56ee33b5-80f9-4b38-b563-1eee8ceebc36","uuid":"b755ae72-bfd8-4471-976e-c04223c5787f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:14:52.471Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
