{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0e326036f28dc5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015: Experiment comparison for training and pipeline runs\n11\t\n12\t## Step 0 Triage\n13\t\n14\tNot below threshold: the strategy spans three components (Dashboard, Model\n15\tRegistry, Data Science Pipelines) owned by three different teams, so it is not\n16\tS-sized/single-component/single-team. Not documentation-only: the Dashboard and\n17\tModel Registry require code changes. Full decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority | Implementation Type |\n22\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|---------------------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view in the Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 | — |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Confirm Data Science Pipelines run data supports run comparison | Implementation | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 | — |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Run lineage on registered model versions | Implementation | Model Registry | Model Registry | P1 | — |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Open run comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 | — |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E005 | Document the run comparison workflow | Implementation | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 | docs-authoring |\n28\t\n29\t## Dependency DAG\n30\t\n31\t```mermaid\n32\tgraph TD\n33\t    E001[\"E001 Run comparison view (Dashboard)\"] --> E004[\"E004 Open comparison from Model Registry\"]\n34\t    E003[\"E003 Run lineage (Model Registry)\"] --> E004\n35\t    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Comparison workflow docs\"]\n36\t    E002[\"E002 Pipelines run-data confirmation\"] --> E005\n37\t    E003 --> E005\n38\t    E004 --> E005\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\tRoots: E001, E002, E003 (all start in parallel).\n42\t\n43\t## DAG Justification\n44\t\n45\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n46\t|------|------|-----------|\n47\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (artifact consumed by code) | The registry entry point builds against the comparison surface (view/route) delivered by the Dashboard comparison work; the consuming implementation is serialized on the producing one. |\n48\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 13 (API/data artifact) | The registry UI consumes the producing-run linkage exposed on model versions; the consuming implementation is serialized on the data-producing epic. |\n49\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring is blocked by every Implementation epic; docs describe what was built. |\n50\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n51\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n52\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n53\t| (no edge) E002 ↔ E001 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Different repos/teams, no shared artifacts. The Dashboard already surfaces pipeline runs and per-run parameters/metrics via the documented KFP v2 interface, so the confirmation runs in parallel; its outcome is an input to follow-up planning, not a gate on the comparison implementation. |\n54\t| (no edge) E003 ↔ E001 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Different repos/components; run lineage capture is independent of the comparison view. |\n55\t| (no edge) E003 ↔ E002 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Different components and repos, no shared artifacts. |\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n58\t\n59\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n60\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n61\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics for two or more selected runs in the Dashboard. |\n62\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E003, RHAISTRAT-9015-E004 | Split along the component boundary: run-lineage data on model versions (Model Registry) and the registry UI entry point that opens the comparison (Dashboard). Both halves are needed for the HLR. |\n63\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 **(bundled)** | Bundled, not split: the \"diff\" view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run parameters/metrics data, in the same component and team as HLR-1. The strategy itself notes requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording. Splitting would build the same surface twice and force an artificial serialization edge; covered at the higher priority (P0) per the redundant-HLR consolidation rule. |\n64\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E005 | Documentation of the comparison workflow from both the runs list and the registry. |\n65\t\n66\tFull coverage: HLR-1 through HLR-4 each map to at least one epic; no orphaned\n67\trequirements and no epic without an HLR (E002 is the passive-component\n68\tvalidation for Data Science Pipelines, supporting HLR-1's pipeline-run scope).\n69\t\n70\t## Health Warnings\n71\t\n72\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n73\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n74\t  no Non-Functional Requirements, and no Technical Approach section. Teams were\n75\t  inferred from the architecture-context owning-team fields\n76\t  (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`). Epic acceptance\n77\t  criteria were derived from the HLRs at a functional level.\n78\t- **Affected Components is a bare list** without change descriptions or owner\n79\t  teams. Active/passive classification was inferred: Dashboard and Model\n80\t  Registry are active (new UI surface; new lineage data on model versions);\n81\t  Data Science Pipelines is passive — the problem statement says parameters and\n82\t  metrics already live in per-run Dashboard pages, and the architecture context\n83\t  documents the KFP v2 REST API with pipeline runs surfaced in the Dashboard,\n84\t  so no DSP code change is expected. Because the passive component is owned by\n85\t  a different team (RHOAI Pipelines) than the nearest active epic's team, its\n86\t  validation is a separate Implementation epic (E002) per the Step 2 exception.\n87\t- **Redundant HLR wording**: HLR-1 and HLR-3 describe one capability (the\n88\t  comparison surface) in two presentation modes; consolidated into E001 at P0\n89\t  rather than split by priority label (see traceability matrix).\n90\t- **E002 priority note**: E002 confirms a P0 capability's data foundation but\n91\t  carries no blocking edge, so priority inheritance does not raise it; it is\n92\t  P1. Risk is low (per-run data is already displayed). If E002 finds gaps,\n93\t  follow-up Data Science Pipelines work will need its own epic — this is a\n94\t  coordination risk, not a dependency.\n95\t- **Out-of-scope consistency**: \"comparison across clusters or across projects\"\n96\t  is out of scope; no epic's scope crosses project or cluster boundaries.\n97\t\n98\t## Tiered Delivery\n99\t\n100\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n101\ttiming; all work is in-platform.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-993eb5c6342419c9","agent_id":"a53b430c9b230258e","session_id":"56ee33b5-80f9-4b38-b563-1eee8ceebc36","uuid":"5335b579-be28-4658-a773-271345897937","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:16:29.524Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0e326036f28dc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
