eria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a model version registered from a known run, then the producing run's\n54\t  reference is recorded on the model version and retrievable through the Model\n55\t  Registry interface by a client that knows only the model version.\n56\t- Given a model version registered without run information, then registration\n57\t  succeeds and the model version remains valid and queryable.\n58\t- Given an existing model version registered before this change, then it\n59\t  remains valid and readable with no migration required.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-2 (P1, data half)**: \"registered model versions link back to the run\n64\t  that produced them\" — the linkage data and its exposure are delivered by\n65\t  this epic. The registry-side entry point that opens a comparison from this\n66\t  linkage is the Dashboard's registry integration and is covered separately.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-993eb5c6342419c9","agent_id":"a53b430c9b230258e","session_id":"56ee33b5-80f9-4b38-b563-1eee8ceebc36","uuid":"dfe8ad46-e70f-42e3-a32e-f87d97f6f9f9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:16:33.635Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85fbb80f4a1e5caa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
